{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your OB-GYN team members. I know you just got transferred from triage. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I’m tired. My mind’s been racing. I haven’t been sleeping. I just… I don’t feel like myself since my dad passed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry about your father. That’s a lot to carry, especially right now. We’ve read your history — you’ve been through a lot with your mood and ECT before. Is that what helped you last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. After the first session, I felt like a fog had lifted. But after Dad died, everything came back — the sadness, the voices… I couldn’t get out of bed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ve already spoken with the ECT team, and they’re planning to restart your treatments. We’ll do them here on Labor and Delivery so we can monitor the baby closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:36:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe for the baby? I keep worrying…"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:37:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a really important question. The risk of untreated severe depression — for both you and the baby — is higher than the risk of ECT. We’ll monitor the fetal heart rate during each treatment, and if anything looks concerning, we’ll stop right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:38:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… that helps. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:39:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your thyroid test came back. Your TSH is high — 9.5 — and your free T4 is low. That means you have hypothyroidism, which can make depression worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know I had that. Could that be part of why I’ve felt so sluggish?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:42:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re starting you on levothyroxine today — 75 micrograms daily. It should help with your energy and mood over the next few weeks. We’ll check your levels again soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-03-02 12:43:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it. I just want to feel stable for my baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-03-03 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling after yesterday’s ECT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-03-03 13:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little groggy still, but… I noticed something. The voices are quieter. Not gone, but not shouting anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-03-03 13:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. The fetal tracing was stable the whole time, so we’re on track for another session in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-03-03 13:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad the baby’s okay. I’ve been so scared I wouldn’t be a good mom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-03-03 13:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing everything you can to take care of yourself — that’s the best thing you can do for your baby. We’re here to support you every step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two more ECT sessions. The psychiatry team says you’re responding well. How’s your mood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I cried yesterday — but it was just… sadness, not despair. I even called my mom. We talked about Dad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a big step. Grieving with support is so important. Your blood pressure has been creeping up though — it was 148/92 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? I’ve been stressed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be pregnancy-induced hypertension. We’re watching it closely. If it gets worse, or if we see protein in your urine, it could be preeclampsia — and we might need to deliver sooner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… I’m not due for another month. Is the baby ready?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-03-07 13:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "At 36 weeks, babies do pretty well. We’d only deliver if it’s safer for you and the baby than continuing the pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-03-10 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is still high — 152/96 — and your urine protein-to-creatinine ratio is elevated. Uric acid is up too. We’re concerned about preeclampsia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-03-10 13:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So… does that mean I’m going to deliver now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-03-10 13:32:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s the safest choice. We’ll start induction today with medication to soften the cervix, then Pitocin. It might take a while, but we’ll support you through it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-03-10 13:33:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I’m scared, but I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-03-13 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi — just checking in. You’ve been in labor for a few days now. Cervix is dilating slowly. Still holding strong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-03-13 14:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired… contractions are intense. But I’m doing my breathing. My boyfriend’s here — he’s helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-03-13 14:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. We’re increasing the Pitocin a bit to help things progress. Baby’s heart rate looks good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-03-15 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re fully dilated! Time to start pushing. You’ve got this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-03-15 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Congratulations — it’s a healthy baby girl! She’s crying strong, Apgar 8 and 9. You did amazing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-03-15 09:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "She’s beautiful… I can’t believe it. I’m a mom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-03-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you are. We did have to do a manual extraction of the placenta — it was retained. But you’re stable, no hemorrhage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-03-15 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that common?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-03-15 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It happens sometimes, especially after a long labor. We’ve given you antibiotics just in case, since there’s a small risk of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-03-16 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-03-16 07:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Sore, especially down there. But happy. I held her for 20 minutes yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-03-16 07:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. You had a second-degree tear — we repaired it. It’ll heal. Any fever or pain beyond the incision?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-03-16 07:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever. Just the usual soreness. I’m taking the ibuprofen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-03-16 07:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Urine culture came back — less than 10,000 organisms, so no infection. We’ll stop the antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry stopped by. They’re really pleased with your mood. You’re clear, engaged — a big change from when you came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still have sad moments, but I’m not trapped in it. I even laughed yesterday when the baby sneezed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s healing. They’re switching you from perphenazine to quetiapine — it’s safer long-term and helps with both mood and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still need ECT after I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-03-18 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, outpatient ECT weekly for now, then tapering. You’ll follow up with your psychiatrist regularly. This plan helped you before — it can again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-03-20 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had another ECT session. How did it go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-03-20 13:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as before — groggy for an hour, then fine. I’m glad I can keep doing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-03-20 13:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And your mood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-03-20 13:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still stable. I’m even thinking about the future — maybe going back to nursing someday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-03-20 13:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great goal. One step at a time. For now, focus on healing and bonding with your baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. Just a few things to go over."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m nervous but ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll keep taking levothyroxine daily — same dose. Get your TSH checked in six weeks. And quetiapine at bedtime — it helps with mood and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:03:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the prenatal vitamins?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep those too — especially important while breastfeeding. And ibuprofen or acetaminophen for pain as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And ECT? When’s my first appointment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:07:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Next week, same day and time as today. Your psychiatrist will coordinate it. And you’ll see them in between for check-ins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:08:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you — for everything. I feel like I have a real chance now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-03-22 09:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You do. You’ve worked so hard. Keep reaching out — to your team, your family, your faith. You’re not alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-03-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick visit — your incision looks great, no signs of infection. You’re cleared for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-03-23 10:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so ready to go home. My mom’s excited to meet the baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-03-23 10:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve come so far — from severe depression, through delivery, to this moment. I’m really proud of you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge. Any questions before we go over the instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just one — if I start feeling down again, what should I do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your psychiatrist right away. Don’t wait. And if you ever feel unsafe, go to the ER. You’re not failing — you’re being proactive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re going home with a solid plan — meds, therapy, ECT, support. You’ve got this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:05:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. For listening. For not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2172-03-24 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Never. Take care of yourself — and that beautiful baby. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your discharge papers are ready. You’re officially going home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can’t believe it. It’s been… a month, almost."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A tough month, but look how far you’ve come. You’re strong, and you’re not alone. Keep leaning on your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:04:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. And congratulations again — on becoming a mom, and on your recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:05:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll call you in a few days to check in. Until then, rest, bond with your baby, and take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:08:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m ready for this next chapter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:09:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And we’re here for it with you. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. Goodbye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:11:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:12:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re all rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2172-03-25 08:15:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That helps more than you know."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-03-02 12:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-03-25 14:12:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with a history of bipolar disorder and recent bereavement was admitted at 35 weeks for recurrent severe depression and akathisia, requiring continuation of electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) during pregnancy. She was found to have new-onset hypothyroidism, which was treated with levothyroxine. After several ECT sessions with good psychiatric response, she developed gestational hypertension and signs of preeclampsia, prompting induction of labor. She delivered a healthy infant via spontaneous vaginal delivery after a prolonged induction, with manual extraction of a retained placenta. Her postpartum course was uncomplicated, with resolution of psychiatric symptoms and stable vital signs. She was discharged home on quetiapine, levothyroxine, and prenatal vitamins, with plans for ongoing outpatient ECT and psychiatric follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Other mental disorders complicating childbirth",
      "Single live birth",
      "Gestational [pregnancy-induced] hypertension without significant proteinuria, third trimester",
      "Unspecified pre-eclampsia, third trimester",
      "Retained placenta without hemorrhage",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "36 weeks gestation of pregnancy",
      "Endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases complicating pregnancy, third trimester",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
